|~ `::keyword` and what is declared under it: its constructor and its
   refusal, and the verbs that turn a keyword into a string, a number
   and a tag.
   The rules it holds: [QSDSP#residence]. ~|

:keyword
  |~~ A keyword is a name that stands for itself, `:name`. It is apart
      from the string so that no name is read by its look: every key of
      a map is a keyword, `/k` reads the field a keyword names, and a
      keyword names a declaration, `:x 5` declaring `x`.

      A bare keyword is a colon and a name that begins with a letter of
      any script or `_` and goes on with letters, digits, `_` and `-`,
      `:id`, `:first-name`; a slash joins names into a path,
      `:domain/user`; any other text is quoted, `:"first name"`, and
      quotes around a bare name change nothing. A keyword is no string,
      `:a | eq "a"` answering `false`, and `toKeyword` and `toString`
      turn one into the other, `"draft" | toKeyword` answering `:draft`. JSON writes a
      keyword as its name, `"draft"`, and keywords rank after regexes
      and before tags.
      ::snippet~(::keyword | manifest) lists its verbs.
      ::link~(::map | doc) ::link~(::string | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/values | doc)
  ~~|
  ::kind
    | wraps |~~ A keyword, read as itself. ~~|
    | throws :PayloadKindNotTakenError
        |~~ `::keyword` reads its payload as the keyword it is; a string
            becomes one by `toKeyword`.
        ~~|
    | proves :isAKeyword
        |~~ `:k` is a keyword. ~~|
        ~(:k | tag | eq ::keyword)
    | proves :buildsAKeyword
        |~~ The constructor of a keyword answers it. ~~|
        ~(::keyword:k | eq :k)
    | proves :takesThreeForms
        |~~ A name of any script, a name with a path and a quoted name are
            keywords alike.
        ~~|
        ~([:данные :domain/user :"$ref"] | map ~toString | eq ["данные" "domain/user" "$ref"])
    | proves :quotesABareName
        |~~ A bare name quoted is the same keyword. ~~|
        ~(:"foo" | eq :foo)
    | proves :PayloadKindNotTakenError/refusesAString
        |~~ A string payload is refused; `toKeyword` turns a string into
            one.
        ~~|
        ~(::keyword"k" !| get [~(tag) /actualTag] | eq [::keyword/PayloadKindNotTakenError ::string])
    | impl ::builtin{}

:keyword/toString
  |~~ Answers the name of the keyword as a string, `:foo | toString`
      answering `"foo"`, the text JSON writes for it, so a key joins text,
      `{:a "x"} | entries | map ~(get [~(get /0 | toString) "=" /1] | join "")`. A
      quoted name and a name with a path answer their text as written,
      `:"foo bar"` the string `"foo bar"`. `toKeyword` turns the string
      back into the keyword.
      ::link~(::string/toKeyword | doc) ::link~(::keyword | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The name of the keyword, a string. ~~| ::string
    | proves :answersTheName
        |~~ A keyword answers its name as written. ~~|
        ~([:foo :"foo bar" :domain/user] | map ~toString | eq ["foo" "foo bar" "domain/user"])
    | proves :readsBack
        |~~ A keyword turned into its name turns back into itself. ~~|
        ~(:baz | toString | toKeyword | eq :baz)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:keyword/toNumber
  |~~ Answers the number the name of the keyword writes,
      `:"1" | toNumber` answering `1`, so a key that `groupBy` filed a
      number under turns back into the number,
      `groupBy /year | keys | toVec | map ~toNumber`. A name that
      writes no number is refused.
      ::link~(::number/toKeyword | doc) ::link~(::string/toNumber | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The number the name writes. ~~| ::number
    | throws :NameNotNumberError
        |~~ `toNumber` reads the name of the keyword as the literal of a
            number, as a key that `groupBy` filed a number under writes
            it, `:"1"`; a name such as `:a` writes none.
        ~~|
    | proves :readsTheNumberOfAKey
        |~~ A key filed from a number turns back into it. ~~|
        ~([{:y 2020} {:y 2021}] | groupBy /y | keys | toVec | map ~toNumber | eq [2020 2021])
    | proves :NameNotNumberError/refusesAName
        |~~ A name that writes no number is refused. ~~|
        ~(:a | toNumber !| tag | eq ::keyword/toNumber/NameNotNumberError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:keyword/toTag
  |~~ Answers the tag the keyword names, `:Box | toTag` answering
      `::Box`; a quoted name that names no tag is refused. `toKeyword`
      turns the tag back into the keyword.
      ::link~(::string/toTag | doc) ::link~(::tag/toKeyword | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The tag the keyword names. ~~| ::tag
    | throws :NameNotTagError
        |~~ `toTag` reads the name of the keyword as the name of a tag; a
            quoted name with a space, `:"a b"`, names none.
        ~~|
    | proves :namesATag
        |~~ A keyword names the tag of its name. ~~|
        ~(:Box | toTag | eq ::Box)
    | proves :NameNotTagError/refusesASpace
        |~~ A name with a space names no tag. ~~|
        ~(:"a b" | toTag !| tag | eq ::keyword/toTag/NameNotTagError)
    | impl ::builtin{}

:keyword/toKeyword
  |~~ Answers the keyword itself, so `map ~toKeyword` turns names,
      strings and numbers into keys, `["a" :b 1] | map ~toKeyword`
      answering `[:a :b :"1"]`.
      ::link~(::string/toKeyword | doc) ::link~(::number/toKeyword | doc)
  ~~|
  ::fn
    | returns |~~ The keyword itself. ~~| ::keyword
    | proves :answersItself
        |~~ A keyword answers itself, so names, strings and numbers turn
            into keys.
        ~~|
        ~(["a" :b 1] | map ~toKeyword | eq [:a :b :"1"])
    | impl ::builtin{}

